$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Non-migration reaction conditions (procedure
A): 6 The appropriate aryl iodide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8 mg, 0.0125
mmol), n-Bu4NCl (0.0694 g, 0.25 mmol), NaHCO3 (0.042 g, 0.5 mmol) and
ethyl acrylate (0.10 g, 1.0 mmol) in DMF (1 ml) under Ar at 100 °C were
stirred for the specified length of time. The reaction mixture was then
cooled to room temperature, diluted with diethyl ether (35 mL) and washed
with brine (30 mL). The aqueous layer was reextracted with diethyl ether
(15 mL). The organic layers were combined, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and
the solvent removed under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on a silica gel column. Ethyl
E-3-(4'-ethoxycarbonylbiphen-2-yl)acrylate (2d). Ethyl 4-(2-
iodophenyl)benzoate (1d) (76.2 mg, 0.25 mmol) was allowed to react for 2
d under nonmigration reaction conditions (procedure A) with ethyl
acrylate. The reaction mixture was chromatographed using 7:1
hexanes/ethyl acetate to afford 58.3 mg (72%) of the indicated compound
(2d) as a clear oil: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.28 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 1.42 (t,
J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 4.21 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 4.42 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 6.41
(d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 7.36- 7.46 (m, 5H), 7.66 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H),
7.70-7.72 (m, 1H), 8.11-8.13 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.3, 14.4, 60.5,
61.1, 119.8, 127.0, 128.3, 129.6, 129.7, 129.9, 130.0, 130.4, 132.7,
141.8, 143.2, 144.5, 166.4, 166.7; IR (CH2Cl2) 2880, 2933, 1713, 1633
cm-1; HRMS m/z 324.1368 (calcd for C20H20O4, 324.1362).
