$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Heck Arylation of
Olefins: An oven-dried carousel reaction tube containing a stirrer bar
was charged with aryl chloride 1 (1.0 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.01 mmol),
4-MeOdppp (0.015 mmol), and KOH (1.5 mmol). After degassing three times
with nitrogen, ethylene glycol (4 mL) and n-butyl vinyl ether 2a (3.0
mmol) were injected sequentially. The reaction mixture was vigorously
stirred at 145 °C for 10 h. After cooling down to room temperature, 2 mL
aqueous HCl (3 M) and 10 mL Et2O were added; the mixture was stirred for
1 h. After separation of the Et2O phase, the aqueous layer was extracted
with Et2O (3 x 10 mL) and the combined organic layers were washed with
brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo (When
aqueous hydrolysis was not necessary, the product was directly extracted
from EG with Et2O). The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of ethyl acetate and hexane
(5/95 to 50/50) as eluant. 1-(Benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)butan-1-one (7b),
yield 72%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.55 (dd, J = 1.6, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.43
(d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 6.83 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.03 (s, 2H), 2.86 (t, J =
7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.78-1.71 (m, 2H), 1.00 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 198.9, 151.9, 148.5, 132.4, 124.6, 108.3, 108.2, 102.2,
40.7, 18.4, 14.3; MS (CI, m/z, %) 210 (100) [M+NH3+H]+; Anal. calcd
forC11H12O3: C, 68.74; H, 6.29. Found: C, 68.82; H, 6.35.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Heck reaction, mechanism studied, carousel reaction tube
used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydrogen-Bonding-Promoted Oxidative Addition and Regioselective Arylation
of Olefins with Aryl Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ruan, Jiwu; Iggo, Jonathan A.; Berry, Neil G.; Xiao, Jianliang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2010), 132(46), 16689-16699

