$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A mixture of PdCl2(MeCN)2
(10 mol%), (S)‐t‐BuPHOX (20 mol%) and dry MeCN (0.05 M) was stirred in a
sealed tube at room temperature for 1 hour under argon. To the resulting
orange solution was added aryl triflate substrate 1 (0.1 mmol),
heterocycle 2 (1.2 equiv) and TMG (5 equiv), the reaction mixture was
heated at 80 °C for 48 hours until the reaction was complete (monitored
by TLC). The solvent was then removed under vacuum and the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel, eluting with ethyl
acetate/petroleum ether 1:3~1:1 (v/v). The products 3.
1,3‐Dimethyl‐3‐((5‐phenyl‐1,3,4‐oxadiazol‐2‐yl)methyl)indolin‐2‐one (3aa)
3‐((5‐(Biphenyl‐4‐yl)‐1,3,4‐oxadiazol‐2‐yl)methyl)‐1‐methyl‐3‐(naphthalen‐1‐yl)indolin‐2‐one
(3nd) According to general procedure, 3nd was obtained in 72% yield (36.5
mg) and 95% ee as a colorless oil. SFC: IB column, 15 ppm MeOH in
supercritical CO2 as eluent, 4 mL/min. Molecular formula: C34H25N3O2;
Molecular Weight: 507.5812 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.92-7.73 (m, 6H),
7.71-7.56 (m, 5H), 7.53-7.43 (m, 4H), 7.41 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 7.38‐7.30
(m, 2H), 7.15 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 6.89 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 4.11 (d, J =
15.2 Hz, 1H), 4.05 (d, J = 15.1 Hz, 1H), 3.28 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 176.9, 164.6, 162.9, 144.4, 143.9, 139.8, 135.6, 133.1, 132.8,
129.7, 129.3, 129.0, 128.7, 128.3, 128.2, 127.6, 127.5, 127.1, 127.1,
126.5, 126.4, 126.0, 125.6, 124.6, 123.0, 122.3, 108.7, 54.7, 33.6, 26.8;
IR: v (cm-1) 3056, 1715, 1613, 1508, 1493, 1486, 1471, 1373, 1348, 1090,
1090, 1016, 1009, 910, 910, 848, 848, 769, 754, 735, 696; HRMS: (ESI)
calcd for C34H25N3O2H+ [M+H]+ 508.2025; found 508.2025. tR = 31 min
(major), 36 min (minor) [α]D 25 = 142.0 (c = 2.0, MeOH) for 95% ee.
