$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S*,E,E)-1-Benzylidene-3-(3-phenyl-2-propenyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene
[(S*,E,E)-16]: In analogy to the typical procedure described for
(R,E,E)-13, Heck reaction of (E,E)-12 (36.5 mg, 0.0750 mmol) with
Pd(OAc)2 (0.84 mg, 0.0037 mmol, 5.0 mol%), (R)-BINAP (3.5 mg, 0.0056
mmol, 7.5 mol%) and K2CO3 (0.042 g, 0.30 mmol) in toluene (0.75 mL) at
80°C for 15 h provided after purification by flash column chromatography
on silica gel (cyclohexane/t-butyl methyl ether 200:1) (S*,E,E)-16 (17.9
mg, 71%) as a colorless oil. The enantiomeric excess was determined by
HPLC analysis (18% ee). As determined from the 1H NMR spectra,
(S*,E,E)-16 was isomerically pure. R f=0.25 (cyclohexane); HPLC (Daicel
Chiracel AD-H, n-heptane/i-PrOH 200:1, flow-rate=0.8 mL/min, λ=295 nm): t
R=11.27 (minor), t R=15.00 (major); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ=7.73 (m, 1
H), 7.33-7.39 (m, 4 H), 7.18-7.30 (m, 8 H), 7.10-7.14 (m, 2 H), 6.37 (d,
J=15.7 Hz, 1 H), 6.17 (ddd, J=15.5, 7.6, 7.6 Hz, 1 H), 3.08 (dd, J=14.5,
3.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.98 (dd, J=16.2, 4.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.63 (dd, J=16.3, 9.7 Hz, 1
H), 2.44 (ddd, J=14.5, 10.3, 2.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.31 (dddd, J=13.9, 6.8, 6.8,
1.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.23 (ddd, J=14.1, 7.2, 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 2.02 (mc, 1 H) ppm;
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ=138.2, 137.7, 137.1, 136.7, 136.2, 131.7,
129.5, 129.4, 128.5, 128.3, 127.6, 127.0, 126.5, 126.5, 126.3, 126.1,
124.4, 124.2, 39.3, 36.3, 35.2, 33.9 ppm; IR (CHCl3): ν=3678, 3015, 2921,
1807, 1700, 1521, 1422, 1216, 967, 928, 801 cm-1; MS (EI): m/z (%): 336
(59) [M+]; elemental analysis calcd (%) for C27H26O: C 92.81, H 7.19;
found: C 92.51, H 6.95.
