$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure A mixture of PdCl2(MeCN)2 (10 mol%), (S)‐t‐BuPHOX (20
mol%) and dry MeCN (0.05 M) was stirred in a sealed tube at room
temperature for 1 hour under argon. To the resulting orange solution was
added aryl triflate substrate 1 (0.1 mmol), heterocycle 2 (1.2 equiv) and
TMG (5 equiv), the reaction mixture was heated at 80 °C for 48 hours
until the reaction was complete (monitored by TLC). The solvent was then
removed under vacuum and the residue was purified by chromatography on
silica gel, eluting with ethyl acetate/petroleum ether 1:3~1:1 (v/v). The
products 3.
1,3‐Dimethyl‐3‐((5‐phenyl‐1,3,4‐oxadiazol‐2‐yl)methyl)indolin‐2‐one (3aa)
According to general procedure, 3aa was obtained in 71% yield (22.5 mg)
and 94% ee as a colorless oil. SFC: AD-H column, 10 ppm MeOH in
supercritical CO2 as eluent, 4 mL/min. Chemical Formula: C19H17N3O2;
Molecular Weight: 319.3572 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.90 (d, J = 6.9
Hz, 2H), 7.58‐7.38 (m, 3H), 7.31‐7.17 (m, 2H), 7.05 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H),
6.83 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 3.48 (d, J = 15.2 Hz, 1H), 3.43 (d, J = 15.2
Hz, 1H), 3.27 (s, 3H), 1.59 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 178.8,
164.7, 163.2, 143.0, 131.6, 129.0, 128.6, 126.7, 123.7, 123.2, 122.8,
108.3, 46.8, 33.3, 26.4, 23.6; IR: v (cm‐1) 2972, 2929, 2900, 1711, 1613,
1569, 1552, 1493, 1470, 1450, 1422, 1378, 1350, 1254, 1125, 1066, 1012,
908; HRMS: (ESI) calcd for C19H17N3O2Na+ [M+Na]+ 342.1218; found
342.1219. tR = 6 min (major), 8 min (minor). [α]D 29 = 30 (c = 1.7, MeOH)
for 94% ee.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, 94% ee; optimized on
Pd-catalyst, ligand, base, substrate and temperature, in-situ generated
catalyst (stage 1), optimization study, sealed tube used
