$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the Alder ene
reaction: To a solution of borylated alkyne (21 mg, 0.12 mmol) and alkene
(14 mg, 0.10 mmol) in acetone (0.2 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere was
added RuCp(CH3CN)3PF6 (4 mg, 0.010 mmol). The reaction was stirred at
room temperature for approximately 2 hours, after which time the solvent
was removed in vacuo and the residue was purified by silica gel
chromatography (hexane:ether 5:1). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.43 (m,
3H), 4.20 (q, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 4.04 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2H), 3.29 (d, J =
14.0 Hz, 1H), 2.84 (d, J = 14.0 Hz, 1H), 2.04 (m, 2H), 2.03 (s, 3H), 1.66
(p, J= 8.0 Hz, 2H), 1.25 (s, 12H), 1.19 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H), 0.87 (s,
9H), 0.00 (s, 3H), -0.01 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.30,
166.95, 130.71, 129.69, 82.83, 72.08, 66.03, 64.20, 34.98, 29.00, 28.59,
26.11, 25.08, 24.96, 23.99, 21.26, 18.44, 15.46, -4.51, -4.72; HRMS (ESI)
calcd for C24H45BO5Si[M+Na]+: 475.3027, found 475.3024.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of β,β-Disubstituted Vinyl Boronates via the
Ruthenium-Catalyzed Alder Ene Reaction of Borylated Alkynes and Alkenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hansen, Eric C.; Lee, Daesung
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(10), 3252-3253

