$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Meso-dibutenanilide 9. A solution of Pd2(dba)3•CHCl3 (0.35 g, 0.34 mmol),
P(2-furyl)3 4 (0.62 g, 2.68 mmol) and 1-methyl-2-pyrrolidinone (NMP) (8
mL) was charged to a basewashed, sealable reaction flask and sparged with
Ar for 1 h. In a separate flask, a solution of diiodide 7 (0.40 g, 0.67
mmol) and stannane 8 (1.75 g, 2.01 mmol) in NMP (5 mL) was sparged with
Ar for 1 h then transferred to the catalyst solution. The resulting dark
yellow solution was degassed using the freeze-pump-thaw technique (3 ×
cycles, -78 °C cooling bath, 0.05 mm, backfilled with Ar). CuI5 (0.38 g,
2.01 mmol) was added in one portion under positive Ar flow and the flask
was sealed. The solution was maintained at rt for 36 h, at which time it
was partitioned between an aqueous solution of NH4OH (30 mL, 20%), brine
(15 mL) and EtOAc (60 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3
× 60 mL) and the combined organic layers were washed with brine (2 × 50
mL). The combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4), filtered and
concentrated. The residue was purified on silica gel using gradient
elution (97:3:0 → 90:10:0 → 85:14:1 CH2Cl2-MeOH-NH4OH) to yield 0.71 g
(71%) of dibutenanilide 9 as a colorless foam. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3)
complex due to the presence of multiple conformations on the NMR
time-scale, see attached spectra; 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) complex due to
the presence of multiple conformations on the NMR time-scale, see
attached spectra δ 169.6, 169.3, 168.9, 146.3, 145.9, 143.6, 143.5,
139.8, 139.1, 136.4, 135.9, 134.4, 134.3, 133.2, 132.7, 131.5, 130.6,
130.3, 129.9, 129.8, 129.8, 129.5, 128.9, 128.8, 128.7, 128.4, 128.2,
128.1, 127.7, 127.2, 126.9, 125.2, 124.3, 121.8, 121.5, 119.8, 118.3,
117.3, 116.5, 83.0, 63.1, 54.4, 52.7, 51.7, 49.4, 38.1, 35.6, 35.3, 34.8,
21.7, 21.6; IR (film) 3401, 2930, 1652, 1424, 1216, 1139, 737 cm-1; LRMS
(ESI) m/z 1507 (1507 calcd for C74H73F6N8O12S4, M+H), 753 (1/2M).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, in-situ generated reagent, Stille cross-coupling reaction
