$DATUM Representative procedure for the Alder ene reaction: To a solution of
borylated alkyne (21 mg, 0.12 mmol) and alkene (14 mg, 0.10 mmol) in
acetone (0.2 mL) under a nitrogen atmosphere was added RuCp(CH3CN)3PF6 (4
mg, 0.010 mmol). The reaction was stirred at room temperature for
approximately 2 hours, after which time the solvent was removed in vacuo
and the residue was purified by silica gel chromatography (hexane:ether
5:1). 8:1 mixture of cis:trans isomers as a colorless oil, yield 21.5 mg,
70%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.45 (m, 2H), 5.14 (s, 1H), 4.06 (t, J =
6.8 Hz, 2H), 3.08 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 2H), 2.08 (m, 2H), 2.05 (s, 3H), 1.83
(d, J = 1.2 Hz, 3H), 1.70 (p, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 1.26 (s, 12H); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.36, 161.57, 130.40, 129.53, 82.80, 64.20, 39.76, 29.02,
28.57, 26.41, 25.00, 21.18; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C17H29BO4 [M+Na]+:
331.2057, found 331.2042.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, 8:1 mixt. of cis:trans isomers, isomers
not sepd.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of β,β-Disubstituted Vinyl Boronates via the
Ruthenium-Catalyzed Alder Ene Reaction of Borylated Alkynes and Alkenes
