$DATUM General Procedure for the Heck Arylation of Olefins: An oven-dried
carousel reaction tube containing a stirrer bar was charged with aryl
chloride 1 (1.0 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.01 mmol), 4-MeOdppp (0.015 mmol), and
KOH (1.5 mmol). After degassing three times with nitrogen, ethylene
glycol (4 mL) and n-butyl vinyl ether 2a (3.0 mmol) were injected
sequentially. The reaction mixture was vigorously stirred at 145 °C for
10 h. 1-(1-(4-Methoxyphenyl)vinyl)pyrrolidin-2-one (4a), Yield 70%. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CD2Cl2) δ 7.27 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 6.87 (d, J = 8.8 Hz,
2H), 5.23 (s, 1H), 5.08 (s, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.56 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 2H),
2.47 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 2.12-2.06 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CD2Cl2) δ
175.0, 160.7, 144.6, 129.7, 128.3, 114.4, 107.4, 56.1, 50.7, 32.7, 19.4;
MS (CI, m/z, %) 218 (100) [M+H]+; Anal. calcd forC13H15NO2: C, 71.87; H,
6.96; N, 6.45. Found: C, 71.80; H, 6.99; N, 6.55.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Heck reaction, mechanism studied, carousel reaction tube
used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydrogen-Bonding-Promoted Oxidative Addition and Regioselective Arylation
of Olefins with Aryl Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
