$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative pr°Cedure for Enaminone
Arylation: Enaminone (0.20 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (14 mg, 0.06 mmol), anhydrous
Cu(OAc)2 powder (110 mg, 0.60 mmol) and granular K2CO3 (55 mg, 0.40
mmol,)5 were combined in a 20:5:1 mixture of t-BuOH/AcOH/DMSO (2.0 mL)
under N2 6 and stirred for 5 min (Note: Solvents were used without
purification or degassing). The reaction mixture was heated to 60 °C and
the potassium trifluoroborate (0.40-0.60 mmol) was added slowly over 5 h
as a solid. The amount of trifluoroborate needed depends on the rate of
addition. Typically 0.20 equivalents of trifluoroborate were added every
30 minutes. The reaction was stirred for an additional h and was
monitored by TLC using 100% EtOAc as the mobile phase. The reaction
mixture was diluted with EtOAc (8 mL) and excess K2CO3 (~1 g) was added
to neutralize the AcOH. After stirring this mixture for 5 min the
precipitate was filtered over Celite using EtOAc as the eluent. The
filtrate was concentrated and purified by chromatography on silica gel
(EtOAc/hexanes).
6-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-2,3,8,8a-tetrahydroindolizin-7(1H)-one (4b).
Trifluoroborate 2 was added slowly over 8 h and the reaction was stirred
for an additional h. 4b was isolated as a pale yellow solid (mp 118-119
°C). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.68- 1.76 (m, 1H), 1.92-2.02 (m, 1H),
2.11-2.15 (m, 1H), 2.28-2.33 (m, 1H), 2.49 (t, 1H, J = 16.0 Hz), 2.58
(dd, 1H, J = 5.0, 16.0 Hz), 3.53-3.63 (m, 2H), 3.79-3.87 (m, 1H), 3.79
(s, 3H), 6.85 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.30 (d, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz), 7.38 (s,
1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 24.4, 33.1, 42.4, 49.8, 55.4, 57.8,
109.5, 113.5 (2C), 128.8 (2C), 129.6, 148.8, 157.4, 189.0; IR (neat)
2953, 2885, 2833, 1620, 1574, 1510, 1277, 837, 733 cm-1; HRMS (ESI+) m/e
calc'd for [M+H]+ C15H18NO2: 244.1338, found 244.1327.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, incremental addition, solvents used without purification
or degassing
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium(II)-Catalyzed Direct Arylation of Enaminones Using
Organotrifluoroborates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
