$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Experimental Procedure for the Heck
Reaction. In a glovebox (vide supra), PdCl2(DBPF) or Pd(tBu3P)2 (2 mol %
relative to aryl bromide), TBAC (45.8 mg, 0.17 mmol),
4,4'-di-tert-butylbiphenyl (44 mg, 0.17 mmol, internal standard), Cy2NMe
(530 μL, 2.47 mmol), aryl bromide (1.65 mmol), and alkene (1.2 or 2 equiv
relative to aryl bromide) were dissolved in N,N-dimethylacetamide (3.00
mL), and the resulting mixture was heated to 80°C for 24 h unless
otherwise stated. The mixture was then cooled to rt, diluted with methyl
tert-butyl ether (25 mL), washed with water (2 x 25 mL), dried (Na2SO4 or
MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo to afford the crude product, which was
purified by FCC. (E)-3-(3-Hydroxyphenyl)but-2-enoic Acid Methyl Ester 17r
as a pale yellow solid, yield 188 mg, 59%. mp 50-51°C (CH2Cl2/i-hexane);
νmax (film) 3381 (br m), 1687 (s), 1622 (s), 1579 (m), 1435 (s), 1351
(m), 1294 (m), 1171 (s) cm-1; δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 2.55 (s, 3H), 3.76 (s,
3H), 6.13 (s, 1H), 6.85 (dd, J = 8.0, 2.5, 1H), 6.93-6.96 (m, 1H), 7.03
(d, J = 7.5, 1H), 7.20-7.27 (m, 1H); δC (100 MHz, CDCl3) 18.0, 51.2,
113.3, 116.0, 116.8, 118.7, 129.7, 143.8, 155.7, 155.7, 167.5; m/z (EI+)
192 ([M]+, 10%), 160 (100); HRMS-GCT m/z [M+] calcd for C11H12O3
192.0786, found 192.0780.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
