$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 21a from Methoxy Acetal 20a (eq 11) Anhydrous cobalt(II)
chloride (55 mg, 0.42 mmol) and DPPH (195 mg, 0.43 mmol) were stirred in
diethyl ether (10 mL) at room temperature for 45 min under argon. The
bromide 20a (0.74 g, 3.6 mmol) in diethyl ether (2 mL), p-methoxystyrene
(0.48 g, 3.6 mmol) and trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium chloride (2 M in
diethyl ether, 5.4 mL, 10.8 mmol) were then added to the [CoCl2(dpph)]
complex. The resulting mixture was then heated under reflux overnight.
The mixture was then allowed to cool to room temperature and then poured
into a saturated solution of aqueous ammonium chloride (20 mL).
Extraction, concentration, and purification on silica gel, using 10% Et2O
in hexane as eluent, provided 21a (0.611 g, 2.5 mmol, 68%) as a colorless
oil. The product 21a consisted of two diastereoisomers (trans/cis =
61:39), judging from the 1H NMR signals of their anomeric protons. The
mixture was partly separated by column chromatography with a solvent
gradient ranging from 2 to 10% Et2O in hexane, to provide trans-21a (209
mg, 0.84 mmol, 23%). No attempts were made to isolate cis-21a.
2-Methoxy-3-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]-1-oxacyclohexane (21a),
yield 0.611 g, 2.5 mmol, 68%
2-Methoxy-3-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]-1-oxacyclohexane (21a,
cis-21a: Rf = 0.38, 10% Et2O in hexane; trans-21a: Rf = 0.34, 10% Et2O in
hexane): trans-21a: IR (neat) 2939, 1608, 1512, 1251, 1174, 1130, 1076,
1033, 962 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.50-1.61 (m, 2H), 1.69-1.75
(m, 1H), 1.99-2.04 (m, 1H), 2.31-2.73 (m, 1H), 3.46 (s, 3H), 3.48-3.55
(m, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.96-4.01 (m, 1H), 4.24 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1H), 6.17
(dd, J = 15.5, 7.0 Hz, 1H) 6.42 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (d, J = 9.0
Hz, 2H), 7.31 (d, J= 9.0 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125.6 MHz) δ 24.7,
25.1, 44.6, 55.0, 55.4, 59.2, 100.9, 113.9, 127.3, 129.0, 129.7, 130.4,
158.9; Found: C, 72.34, H, 8.18%. Calcd for C15H20O3: C, 72.55, H, 8.12%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, trans:cis 61:39, mixture of isomers
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cobalt-Catalyzed Trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium-Promoted Radical
Alkenylation of Alkyl Halides: A Complement to the Heck Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Affo, Walter; Ohmiya, Hirohisa; Fujioka, Takuma; Ikeda, Yousuke;
Nakamura, Tomoaki; Yorimitsu, Hideki; Oshima, Koichiro; Imamura, Yuki;
Mizuta, Tsutomu; Miyoshi, Katsuhiko
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
