$DATUM rac-syn-(E)-t-Butyl
3-(2-(N-(cyclohex-2-enyl)acetamido)-3,5-dimethylphenyl)acrylate
(syn-25b): To a solid mixture of Pd2(dba)3.CHCl3 (0.041 g, 0.040 mmol)
and P(t-Bu)3.HBF4 (0.046 g, 0.160 mmol) was added degassed DMF (2.0 mL)
via syringe. The mixture was stirred for 10 min, at which point syn-9b
(0.148 g, 0.40 mmol) was added as a solid all at once, followed by
t-butyl acrylate (0.205 g, 1.60 mmol) via syringe. Finally, Et3N (0.061
mg, 0.600 mmol) was added via syringe, and the mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 24 h. The mixture was quenched with brine (5 mL) and
extracted with Et2O (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated by rotary evaporation. Column
chromatography (2:1 hexanes:EtOAc) furnished the title compound (0.102 g,
69%) as a clear colorless oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.70 (d, J =
15.9 Hz, 1H), 7.33 (s, 1H), 7.13 (s, 1H), 6.26 (d, J = 15.9 Hz, 1H), 5.97
(m with clear d, J = 9.9 Hz, 1H), 5.73 (dq, J = 9.6 Hz, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 4.91
(m, 1H), 2.36 (s, 3H), 2.21 (s, 3H), 1.95-1.85 (m, 2H), 1.75-1.40 (m,
3H), 1.68 (s, 3H), 1.53 (s, 9H), 1.27-1.12 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 170.7, 165.6, 139.9, 138.1, 137.4, 137.2, 134.2, 133.4, 128.8,
128.6, 125.2, 122.4, 80.5, 54.4, 28.1 (3C), 26.3, 24.6, 23.2, 21.4, 21.0,
18.5; FTIR (neat, cm-1) 2976, 2932, 1708, 1656, 1472, 1370, 1328, 1303,
1256, 1154, 983, 919, 855, 731; LRMS (EI) m/z 369 (M+, 11), 312 (25), 270
(100), 252 (25), 174 (43), 158 (30), 121 (25), 81 (58); HRMS (EI) calcd
for C23H31NO3: 369.2304, found: 369.2289.
