$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Optically Pure (2S,3S)-23c (eq 14) Anhydrous cobalt(II)
chloride (13 mg, 0.10 mmol) and DPPH (54 mg, 0.12 mmol) were stirred in
diethyl ether (10 mL) at room temperature for 45 min under argon. The
enantiomerically pure (2S,3R)- 22c (0.30 g, 1.0 mmol) in diethyl ether (2
mL), p-methoxystyrene (133 mg, 1.0 mmol) and
trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium chloride (2 M in diethyl ether, 1.5 mL, 3.0
mmol) were then added to the [CoCl2(dpph)] complex. The whole mixture was
then heated under reflux for 6 h. After being quenched with a saturated
ammonium chloride solution (20 mL), the organic layer was partitioned.
The organic extract was dried and concentrated in vacuo. The residue
which was obtained as a mixture of two diastereoisomers was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel, using 2% diethyl ether in hexane as
eluent, to provide 23c (242 mg, 0.68 mmol, 68%) as a colorless oil. The
product 23c was a mixture of two diastereoisomers ((2S,3S)/(2S,3R) >
97:3), judging from the 1H NMR signals of their anomeric protons. The
mixture was partly separated by column chromatography with 2% Et2O in
hexane, to provide (2S,3S)-23c (108 mg, 0.30 mmol, 30%). No attempts were
made to isolate (2S,3R)-23c.
2-Isomenthoxy-3-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]-1-oxacyclopentane (23c),
yield 242 mg, 0.68 mmol, 68%
2-Isomenthoxy-3-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]-1-oxacyclopentane (23c,
(2S,3R)-23c: Rf = 0.34, 5% Et2O in hexane; (2S,3S)-23c: Rf = 0.33, 5%
Et2O in hexane): (2S,3S)-23c: IR (neat) 2869, 1608, 1577, 1512, 1463,
1367, 1296, 1249, 1174, 1035, 966, 750 cm-1; [α]D 20= -16.8 (CHCl3, c =
0.10); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 0.83 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.91 (dd, J =
13.0, 6.5 Hz, 6H), 1.19-1.26 (m, 2H), 1.33-1.43 (m, 2H), 1.53-1.59 (m,
3H), 1.74-1.93 (m, 3H), 2.24-2.31 (m, 1H), 2.90 (q, J = 14.0, 6.0 Hz,
1H), 3.65 (q, J = 11.5, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.99 (dd, J = 7.5, 6.0
Hz, 2H), 4.96 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 6.00 (dd, J = 16.0, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 6.41
(d, J = 15.5 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 7.29 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H);
13C NMR (CDCl3, 125.6 MHz) δ 19.0, 20.4, 20.7, 21.2, 25.8, 27.6, 30.2,
31.4, 38.0, 46.5, 49.4, 55.3, 66.6, 75.0, 108.3, 114.0, 127.3, 127.9,
130.0, 130.1, 159.0; Found: C, 76.83, H, 9.78%. Calcd for C23H34O3: C,
77.05, H, 9.56%.
