$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 21b from Isopropoxy Acetal 20b (eq 11) Anhydrous cobalt(II)
chloride (29 mg, 0.22 mmol) and DPPH (122 mg, 0.27 mmol) were stirred in
diethyl ether (10 mL) at room temperature for 45 min under an atmosphere
of argon. The bromide 20b (0.50 g, 2.12 mmol) in diethyl ether (2 mL),
p-methoxystyrene (0.30 g, 2.25 mmol) and trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium
chloride (2 M in diethyl ether, 3.4 mL, 6.8 mmol) were then charged. The
whole mixture was refluxed for 8 h. Workup followed by chromatographic
purification with 5% Et2O in hexane as eluent gave 21b (0.397 g, 1.44
mmol, 68%). The product 21b was a mixture of two diastereoisomers
(trans/cis = 69:31), judging from the 1H NMR signals of their anomeric
protons. The mixture was chromatographed again with a solvent gradient
ranging from 1 to 5% Et2O in hexane to provide trans- 21b (180 mg, 0.65
mmol, 31%). No attempts were made to isolate cis-21b
2-Isopropoxy-3-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]-1-oxacyclohexane (21b),
yield 0.397 g, 1.44 mmol, 68%)
2-Isopropoxy-3-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]-1-oxacyclohexane (21b,
cis-21b: Rf = 0.36, 10% Et2O in hexane; trans-21b: Rf = 0.34, 10% Et2O in
hexane): trans-21b: IR (neat) 2968, 1608, 1512, 1442, 1296, 1251, 1174,
1072, 1010, 966, 846 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.14 (d, J = 6.0 Hz,
3H), 1.25 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H), 1.48-1.72 (m, 3H), 2.00-2.08 (m, 1H),
2.28-2.34 (m, 1H), 3.47-3.52 (m, 1H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.95 (m, 1H),
3,98-4.02 (m, 1H), 4.34 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 6.16 (dd, J = 16.0, 7.0 Hz,
1H), 6.40 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.30 (d, J =
8.5 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125.6 MHz) δ 21.8, 23.6, 24.1, 27.4, 43.5,
55.3, 64.5, 70.0, 102.0, 113.9, 127.2, 128.2, 129.7, 130.6, 158.8; Found:
C, 73.66, H, 9.04%. Calcd for C17H24O3: C, 73.88, H, 8.75%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, trans:cis 69:31, mixture of isomers
