$DATUM (E)-N-tert-Butyl-cyclobutyl penta-2,4-dienamide (entry 7). Lithium
chloride (169.6 mg, 4.00 mmol), X-Phos (9.6 mg, 0.02 mmol),
1-cyclobutylvinyl diphenylphosphate (198.2 mg, 0.60 mmol), N-tert-butyl
acrylamide (50.9 mg, 0.40 mmol), Cy2NMe (170 μL, 0.80 mmol), PdCl2(COD)
(5.7 mg, 0.02 mmol) dissolved in a 1:1 DMF-Dioxane mixture (3 mL) were
reacted for 24 h at 100°C. The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel using CH2Cl2 as eluent. This afforded 56 mg
of the title compound (68 % yield) as a colorless solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CD2Cl2) δ (ppm) 6.99 (d, 1H, J = 15.6 Hz), 5.69 (d, 1H, J = 15.6 Hz),
5.55 (bs, 1H, NH), 5.23 (m, 1H), 5.14 (m, 1H), 3.06 (m, 1H), 2.15-2.08
(m, 2H), 1.92-1.82 (m, 4H), 1.28(m, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CD2Cl2) 165.4,
148.6, 140.7, 122.7, 118.6, 51.3, 37.4, 28.7, 28.1, 18.5. Mass confirmed
by GCMS analysis.
