Hydrolysis Producing 4. The reactants were added to a reaction vial in
the following order: aryl iodide or aryl bromide 2 (0.60 mmol), enol
ether 6a (0.78 mmol, 0.152 g), Pd(OAc)2 (0.018 mmol, 0.004 g), NaOAc
(0.72 mmol, 0.059 g), LiCl (1.20 mmol, 0.051 g), K2CO3 (0.72 mmol, 0.100
g), DMF (2 mL) and water (0.2 mL). The tube was closed and the contents
were magnetically stirred and heated for 1-3 days at 70-100 °C (Table 1).
The reaction was interrupted when GC-MS analysis showed no further
improvements in conversion. After cooling, 0.5 mL concd HCl was added and
the contents stirred for 30 min. After full hydrolysis (GC-MS) the
reaction mixture was diluted with 10 mL 0.5 M HCl and extracted five
times with diethyl ether. The ethereal phases were washed twice with 0.1
M NaOH and dried with K2CO3(s). Evaporation of the solvent and silica
column chromatography. Pure products 4.
(R)-2-(2-Methoxy-phenyl)-2-methyl-cyclopentanone (4a) 2 Compound 4a was
obtained in 67% yield and 98% ee after silica column chromatography
(hexane-diethyl ether, 70:30). HPLC OD-H (isohexane/2-propanol 99.5:0.5):
flowrate = 0.4 mL/min. tr = 52 min (+), tr = 57 min (-); [α] D 23 = +39°
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, KEY STEP, enantioselective, 98% ee
