$DATUM A mixture of 26c (41.8 mg, 0.10 mmol), PdCl2 (2 mg, 0.01 mmol, 10 mol%),
PPh3 (5 mg, 0.02 mmol, 20 mol%), Cs2CO3 (82 mg, 0.25 mmol, 2.5 eq),
norbornene (57 mg, 0.6 mmol, 6.0 eq), 8a (0.121 g, 0.6 mmol, 6.0 eq) in
1,4-dioxane (1.0 ml) in a schlenk tube was stirred at 85°C for 20 h.
After being cooled to room temperature the mixture was filtered through a
plug of Celite eluting with ethyl acetate (3×10 ml). The filtrate was
washed with brine (10 ml), dried over sodium sulfate, and concentrated.
The crude product was purified by column chromatography (10% ethyl
acetate/ hexanes then 50% hexanes/ dichloromethane). 27c (27.1 mg, 66 %).
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.45 (s, 1 H), 7.83 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H),
7.58-7.41 (m, 3 H), 6.79 (s, 1 H), 5.80 (dd, J = 16.4, 10.4 Hz, 1 H),
5.15 (s, 1 H), 4.92-4.80 (m, 1 H), 4.74 (bs, 1 H), 4.73 (d, J = 17.2 Hz,
1 H), 4.10 (t, J = 9.2 Hz, 1 H), 2.18 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H), 2.15-2.00 (m,
1 H), 2.00-1.84 (m, 2 H), 1.84-1.56 (m, 3 H), 1.17-1.05 (m, 6 H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 179.0, 172.5, 149.9, 139.1, 133.5, 131.5, 130.7,
130.6, 128.4, 125.8, 124.1, 118.2, 115.4, 67.6, 46.1, 43.0, 32.0, 30.0,
29.5, 21.70, 21.67, 18.3; HRMS (ACPI) calcd for C23H27O5N2 [M++H]
411.1915, found 411.1922.
