$DATUM (E)-N-tert-Butyl-4-methyl penta-2,4-dienamide (entry 1+2). Lithium
chloride (169.6 mg, 4.00 mmol), X-Phos (9.6 mg, 0.02 mmol), propen-2-yl
diphenylphosphate (174.0 mg, 0.60 mmol), N-tert-butyl acrylamide (50.9
mg, 0.40 mmol), Cy2NMe (170 μL, 0.80 mmol), PdCl2(COD) (5.7 mg, 0.02
mmol) dissolved in a 1:1 DMF-Dioxane mixture (3 mL) were reacted for 72 h
at 100°C. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography on
silica gel using CH2Cl2 as eluent. This afforded 43 mg of the title
compound (65% yield) as a colorless solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3CN) δ
(ppm) 7.14 (d, 1H, J = 15.6 Hz), 6.38 (bs, 1H, NH), 5.99 (d, 1H, J = 15.6
Hz), 5.30 (t, 1H, J = 0.8 Hz), 5.27 (s, 1H), 1.88 (s, 3H), 1.35 (s, 9H).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CD3CN) 166.0, 142.0, 141.9, 124.5, 122.4, 51.6, 28.9,
18.5. HRMS C10H17NO [M+Na+]: 190.1208 found: 190.1209.
