$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: vi) Procedures for the synthesis of product 4.
0.2 mmol (1 equiv) of enamide, 4.5 mg (0.02 mmol, 10 mol%) of palladium
(II) acetate and 6.0 mg (0.02 mmol, 10 mol%) of Johnphos, Na3PO4 (65.6
mg, 2.0equiv), 55.8 mg (1.0 equiv) tetrabutylammonium chloride and AdCOOH
(10.8 mg, 30 mol%) were dissolved in 2 mL of dry DMF in a screw cap vial
under argon atmosphere. And the vial was heated at 110 °C under the
atmosphere of Ar for 24 h. The solution was diluted with EA, washed by
ammonium chloride saturated solution. The organic layer was concentrated
in vacuum and the product was isolated through flash column
chromatography (hexane/ethyl acetate = 3:1 ) to give the desired product.
ethyl 3-oxo-2,3,5,9b-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolo[2,1-a]isoindole-9b-carboxylate
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.37-7.35 (m, 1H), 7.30 – 7.19 (m, 3H), 4.89
(d, J = 14.8 Hz, 1H), 4.32 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 1H), 4.15 – 4.02 (m, 2H),
3.04-2.99 (m, 1H), 2.81-2.70 (m, 1H), 2.35-2.21 (m, 2H), 1.15 (t, J = 7.1
Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 176.85, 172.13, 140.75, 139.06,
128.90, 128.03, 123.12, 122.64, 77.29, 61.97, 48.73, 33.00, 32.77, 14.02.
HRMS (ESI): m/z calculated for C14H15NO3Na [M+Na]+:268.0950 found:
268.0951.
