$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Indanones
(II). To an oven-dried, 2-5 mL Biotage microwave vial with microstirrer
is added carbonyl-ene product (0.08 mmol, 1 equiv),
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (2 equiv) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1 mol%). The
vial is capped with a crimp-cap and heated to 150 °C for 20-25 minutes in
a Biotage microwave reactor. The reaction is diluted with an equal volume
of diethyl ether and poured into a separatory funnel. The ethereal layer
is washed with a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (2 x 2 mL). The aqueous
washes are back extracted with diethyl ether (1 X 4 mL). The organic
fractions are combined and washed with brine (1 x 2 mL), dried with
anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude products
are purified via column chromatography on silica gel.
(S)-1-(3-methoxy-1-phenyl-1H-inden-2-yl)ethanone (10) Compound 10 was
prepared according to the general procedure (II) using (9)-
(R,Z)-3-((2-bromophenyl)(methoxy)methyl)-4- phenylbut-3-en-2-one (25 mg,
0.072 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (~0.5 mg, 1 mol%) and 1,2,2,6,6-
pentamethylpiperidine (27 μL, 0.145 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL). The crude
material was purified by column chromatography (15% Ethyl
Acetate:hexanes) to give the title compound as a colorless oil (12 mg,
65%). 14% ee by HPLC using Chiralcel OJ, 1 mL/min, 0.3% 2-propanol in
hexane tR = 24.73 (minor) and 33.58 (major) min (UV 254 nm). FTIR (film)
1653, 1591, 1559, 1540, 1378, 1258 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.69
(d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 7.32 (m, 2H), 7.24 (m, 2H), 7.19 (m, 2H), 7.12 (d, J
= 7.0 Hz, 2H), 4.85 (s, 1H), 4.29 (s, 3H), 2.32 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ 194.6, 165.3, 148.4, 139.6, 137.3, 129.3, 128.6(2C),
127.5(2C), 127.1, 126.8, 125.9, 125.0, 121.9, 60.7, 52.3, 30.5 ppm. MS
(ESI) m/z calcd for [M+Na]+ (C18H16O2Na)+: 287 Found: [M+Na]+ 287.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of Substituted Indanones from Silyloxyallenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
