$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the 1,4-palladium alkyl
to aryl migration. A mixture of aryl halide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8
mg, 0.0125 mmol), bis(diphenylphosphino)methane (4.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol),
cesium pivalate (0.1170 g, 0.5 mmol), and the indicated amounts of alkene
(if employed) in dry DMF (4 mL) was quickly flushed with argon and
stirred at the indicated reaction temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC and gas chromatographic analysis. After the reaction was complete,
it was diluted with ethyl ether, washed with satd aq NaHCO3, dried over
Na2SO4, concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
Ethyl (2E)-3-(4,4-dimethyl-3,4-dihydro-2H-chromen-5-yl)propenoate (25).
Compound 24 (68.5 mg, 0.25 mmol) and ethyl acrylate (0.375 mmol) were
allowed to react under our standard reaction conditions for 18 h. The
reaction mixture was diluted with diethyl ether (30 mL) and washed with
brine (30 mL). The organic layer was dried (Na2SO4), filtered and the
solvent removed under reduced pressure. The residue was chromatographed
(8:1 hexane/EtOAc) to afford 40.3 mg of the indicated compound (62 %
yield) as a yellow oil: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.34 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.46
(s, 6H), 1.84 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 4.15 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 4.27 (q, J =
7.2 Hz, 2H), 6.18 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 6.84 (dd, J = 1.5, 7.5 Hz, 1H),
6.98-7.10 (m, 2H), 8.32 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.5,
30.4, 31.6, 41.1, 60.7, 62.5, 119.5, 119.6, 121.6, 127.4, 129.9, 136.0,
146.3, 154.7, 169.2; IR (CHCl3, cm-1) 3018, 2966, 1712; HRMS Calcd for
C16H20O3: 260.1412. Found: 260.1416.
