$DATUM (3aS,3a'R,3a''S,3a'''S,8aS,8a'R)-Dioxindole 10. A resealable tube was
charged with meso-dibutenanilide 9 (150 mg, 0.10 mmol), (R)-Tol-BINAP
(140 mg, 0.20 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (22.4 mg, 0.10 mmol), CH3CN (2 mL,
previously sparged with Ar for 1 h) and 1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine
(PMP) (70 μL, 0.40 mmol). The heterogeneous red-brown mixture was sparged
with Ar for 45 min at rt. The reaction vessel then was sealed and heated
at 80 °C for 12 h. After cooling to rt, the reaction mixture was
partitioned between an aqueous solution of aqueous NaCN (5 mL, 20%) and
EtOAc (10 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 10 mL),
and the combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4), filtered and
concentrated. The residue was purified on silica gel using gradient
elution (97:3:0 → 90:10:0 → 85:14:1 CH2Cl2-MeOH-NH4OH) to yield 100 mg
(83% combined yield) of 10 and two meso decacyclic products in a 9:2:1
ratio (by HPLC analysis). This mixture could be further purified by
preparative reverse-phase HPLC (Luna 5 μm C18(2), 250 × 21.2 mm, 85:15
MeOH-1% NH4OH in H2O, 1200 psi-12 mL/min, UV detection at 254 nm) to
afford 74 mg (62%) of 10 as colorless foam and 17 mg and 8 mg of two meso
decacyclic products, both as a colorless foams. Dioxindole 10: 90% ee
(HPLC analysis: Chiralcel OD-R, 80:20 CH3CN-NaClO4 0.5 M aqueous, 0.5
mL/min, UV detection at 254 nm). [α]28 D -59.9, [α]28 577 -61.7, [α]28
546 -72.2, [α]28 435 -153, [α]28 405 -207 (c 0.25, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (500
MHz, (CD3)2SO, 100 °C) δ 7.49-7.45 (m, 4H), 7.37-7.24 (m, 15H), 7.09-7.02
(m, 5H), 6.91 (br d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.78-6.70 (m, 2H), 6.64 (d, J =
14.3 Hz, 1H), 6.59 (d, J = 14.3 Hz, 1H), 6.50-6.25 (m, 2H), 5.42 (d, J =
14.3 Hz, 1H), 5.28 (d, J = 14.3 Hz, 1H), 5.05 (d, J = 15.8 Hz, 1H), 4.98
(d, J = 15.5 Hz, 1H), 4.85 (d, J = 15.4 Hz, 1H), 4.78 (d, J = 15.8 Hz,
1H), 4.40-4.10 (m, 3H), 2.87 (s, 3H), 2.83 (s, 3H), 2.70-2.65 (m, 1H),
2.52-2.49 (m, 1H), 2.40 (s, 3H), 2.37 (s, 3H), 2.36-2.30 (m, 2H),
2.26-2.20 (m, 1H), 2.13 (s, 3H), 1.96-1.90 (m, 1H), 1.86-1.82 (m, 1H),
1.77-1.71 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, (CD3)2SO, 100 °C) δ 176.2, 176.0,
149.9, 148.0, 143.4, 143.3, 141.3, 141.2, 135.7, 135.6, 134.5, 133.9,
133.7, 133.4, 130.5, 130.3, 129.7, 129.5, 129.3, 127.9(2), 127.7, 127.6,
127.0, 126.8, 126.7, 126.4, 126.1, 126.0, 125.9, 124.5, 124.1, 122.8,
122.6, 122.1, 121.9, 118.3, 117.3, 116.6, 110.0, 109.8, 109.0, 108.9,
82.2, 62.2, 61.8, 55.7, 50.9, 50.9, 42.8, 42.6, 35.8, 34.3, 33.8, 31.8,
31.7, 28.3, 20.3, 20.2; IR (film) 3354, 2930, 1710, 1610, 1359, 1162, 745
cm-1; LRMS (ESI) m/z 1207, (1207 calcd for C72H71N8O6S2, M+H), 603
(1/2M).
