$DATUM Compound 14. To a dry round bottom flask equipped with a stirrer bar,
compound 12 (100 mg, 0.11 mmol), 4-iodobenzadehyde 13 (26.8 mg, 0.11
mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (10%), Bu4NBr (37.2 mg, 0.11 mmol) and K2CO3 (20.6 mg,
0.15 mmol) were dissolved in dry DMF. The resulting mixture was refluxing
overnight. The solvent was then removed under vacuum and the mixture was
quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl and extracted with CH2Cl2.
The organic extracts were washed with water and dried over MgSO4. The
removal under vacuum of the organic solvent led to the crude product
which was purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel,
hexane/CH2Cl2 1:2) to afford 14 as an orange solid (68.3 mg, 0.07 mmol)
61 % yield. Compound 14, yield (68.3 mg, 0.07 mmol) 61 %. 1H NMR (CDCl3,
300 MHz, 298 K) δ 10.01 (s, 1H, -CHO), 7.90 (d, J= 8.3 Hz, 2H, ArH),
7.70-7.65 (m, 3H, ArH and/or Vinyl), 7.35-7.05 (m, 10H, ArH, Vinyl),
6.75-6.70 (m, 4H, ArH-[2,2]paracyclophane), 6.44 (d, J= 7.8 Hz, 2H,
ArH-[2,2]paracyclophane), 5.79 (dd, J= 17.6 Hz, J= 1.3 Hz, 1H, Vinyl),
5.30 (dd, J= 11.6 Hz, J= 1.3 Hz, 1H, Vinyl), 4.15-4.05 (m, 8H, α -CH2),
3.65-3.55 (m, 2H, [2,2]paracyclophane), 3.16-2.90 (m, 6H,
[2,2]paracyclophane), 2.00- 1.80 (m, 8H, β -CH2), 1.65-1.25 (m, 24H, γ-,
δ-, ε -CH2), 1.00-0.85 (m, 12H, -CH3); 13C RMN (CDCl3, 75 MHz, 298 K) δ
192.0, 151.9, 151.6, 151.5, 151.1, 144.6, 139.8, 139.7, 138.7, 138.6,
138.5, 138.3, 135.4, 133.8, 133.7, 131.9, 130.6, 130.5, 130.4, 128.9,
128.8, 128.2, 127.9, 127.6, 127.5, 127.3, 127.2, 126.0, 125.5, 125.2,
114.4, 111.7, 110.8, 110.7, 70.0, 69.9, 69.8, 69.7, 34.8, 33.9, 32.1,
32.0, 31.3, 30.1, 30.0, 29.9, 29.8, 26.5, 26.4, 26.3, 26.2, 23.1,
23.0(2), 14.5, 14.4; FTIR (neat): 2926, 2857, 1696, 1595, 1565, 1497,
1465, 1421, 1385, 1306, 1255, 1205, 1165, 1122, 1028, 965, 899, 866, 812,
769, 728, 653 cm-1; MALDI-TOF m/z: 969.4 [M+H]+.
